The values are restructured into JSON. The Bank for International Settlements
does not endorse this project.



Varieties of Democracy

The following JSON files are derived from the V-Dem Country-Year Core dataset
and redistributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International license (CC BY-SA 4.0). Adaptations of this data must be shared
under the same license.

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
https://v-dem.net/data/the-v-dem-dataset/

Files:

- data/political_freedom.json

Source: Coppedge, Michael, John Gerring, Carl Henrik Knutsen, Staffan I.
Lindberg, Jan Teorell, David Altman, Fabio Angiolillo, Michael Bernhard, Agnes
Cornell, M. Steven Fish, Linnea Fox, Lisa Gastaldi, Haakon Gjerløw, Adam Glynn,
Ana Good God, Allen Hicken, Katrin Kinzelbach, Joshua Krusell, Kyle L.
Marquardt, Kelly McMann, Valeriya Mechkova, Juraj Medzihorsky, Anja Neundorf,
Pamela Paxton, Daniel Pemstein, Josefine Pernes, Johannes von Römer, Brigitte
Seim, Rachel Sigman, Svend-Erik Skaaning, Jeffrey Staton, Aksel Sundström,
Marcus Tannenberg, Eitan Tzelgov, Yi-ting Wang, Tore Wig, Steven Wilson and
Daniel Ziblatt. 2026. "V-Dem Country-Year Dataset v16" Varieties of Democracy
(V-Dem) Project. https://doi.org/10.23696/vdemds26

The liberal democracy index is scaled from its published 0 to 1 range to a
score from 0 to 100. The values are restructured into JSON. The V-Dem
Institute does not endorse this project.



Wikipedia

The following JSON files are derived from English Wikipedia and redistributed
under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International license
(CC BY-SA 4.0). Adaptations of this data must be shared under the same license.

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_English-speaking_population
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opposition_to_immigration
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sovereign_states_by_immigrant_and_emigrant_population

Files:

- data/english_speaking_population.json
- data/opposition_to_immigration.json
- data/immigrant_population_share.json

The English-speaking percentage is the total share, including people who
speak English as an additional language. The opposition figure is the share
of respondents who want fewer immigrants or none, from the cross-country
survey table on the opposition-to-immigration page. The immigrant share is
the United Nations international migrant stock as a percentage of each
country's population. The values are restructured into JSON. Wikipedia
contributors do not endorse this project.



Heritage Foundation

The following JSON files are taken from the Heritage Foundation Index of
Economic Freedom and redistributed with attribution. The Index is free to
use with attribution. The Heritage Foundation retains its rights in the
Index.

https://www.heritage.org/index/
https://economicfreedom.heritage.org/

Files:

- data/economic_freedom.json
- data/business_freedom.json

The overall score and the business freedom component are copied from the
annual Excel workbooks and restructured into JSON. Scores run from 0 to 100.
The Heritage Foundation does not endorse this project.
